      "id": 4,
      "kind": "mother_usage",
      "payload": "{\"model_calls\":1,\"phase\":\"preparation\",\"plan\":{\"A\":\"Build an OpenMP scaling candidate while retaining the source’s two-phase compute-then-copy state model, isolating thread-level gains. Partition independent rows statically; use an integer logical-OR reduction for the strict error predicate and barriers between stencil, copy, and the next iteration. Preserve arithmetic order, fixed boundaries, degenerate sizes, and stdout exactly; do not introduce in-place updates, unsafe FP flags, runtime/script changes, or hardcoded inputs. Measure full-program performance.\",\"B\":\"Build a separate structural-memory candidate, initially without thread parallelism: replace row allocations with contiguous buffers and eliminate the interior copy sweep by swapping current/next buffers. Initialize both buffers so every boundary and degenerate-grid result matches the original (cloning the full initial field is safest); begin with the original grid as current and overwrite every interior next cell before a swap. Preserve the float-valued threshold, iteration/parity behavior, calculation order, and output format. Report an end-to-end valid candidate.\",\"C\":\"Create isolated source-equivalent whole-program variants for the remaining bottlenecks: a SIMD-friendly ARM64 inner stencil with scalar tails and the same left-associated operations, plus a conservative stdout-path variant using standard-library buffering/locking while retaining libc `%lf ` conversion, order, spaces, and newlines. Keep the original update model and avoid threaded changes so results are independently composable. Do not hand-round values, omit output, reassociate FP operations, or use precomputed/analytic solutions; retain only variants that win end-to-end.\",\"G\":\"Treat A, B, and C outputs as alternatives first. Rebuild and validate each under the unchanged baseline harness, then select the lowest repeated valid full-run mean. Combine only independently validated mechanisms (for example A’s parallelism with B’s swap); after every merge, revalidate and remeasure because cache, synchronization, and serial output can make integration slower. Audit source-specific edge behavior—initial heat region, untouched boundaries, `hasError` initially true, strict comparison to `1.0e-5f`, iteration limit, and exact formatting—and reject any candidate that changes it. Do not alter toolchain, runtime budget, oracle, tests, or target.\",\"analysis\":\"The only measurement is a correct 4-case baseline on 4-core ARM64: 0.067895 s mean (0.067770–0.067971 s), so there is no evidence for a test-size distribution or a measured bottleneck. The executable reference performs a serial stencil sweep plus a full interior copy each iteration, uses separately allocated rows, and emits every cell serially. The strongest generic hypotheses are reduced copy traffic, four-core parallelism/SIMD, and output overhead. Reference behavior comes from the executable code, not prose/comments: preserve inclusive heat initialization, fixed boundaries, Jacobi—not Gauss-Seidel—updates, strict float-threshold semantics, stop control, and byte-compatible output. No specialization, answer substitution, or unsafe numerical transformation is acceptable.\"},\"request_sha256\":\"a4e5e250f6bfdc829da97aa951fc148001c901e3e417b0e389b542b709429a6e\",\"response\":{\"data\":{\"A\":\"Build an OpenMP scaling candidate while retaining the source’s two-phase compute-then-copy state model, isolating thread-level gains. Partition independent rows statically; use an integer logical-OR reduction for the strict error predicate and barriers between stencil, copy, and the next iteration. Preserve arithmetic order, fixed boundaries, degenerate sizes, and stdout exactly; do not introduce in-place updates, unsafe FP flags, runtime/script changes, or hardcoded inputs. Measure full-program performance.\",\"B\":\"Build a separate structural-memory candidate, initially without thread parallelism: replace row allocations with contiguous buffers and eliminate the interior copy sweep by swapping current/next buffers. Initialize both buffers so every boundary and degenerate-grid result matches the original (cloning the full initial field is safest); begin with the original grid as current and overwrite every interior next cell before a swap. Preserve the float-valued threshold, iteration/parity behavior, calculation order, and output format. Report an end-to-end valid candidate.\",\"C\":\"Create isolated source-equivalent whole-program variants for the remaining bottlenecks: a SIMD-friendly ARM64 inner stencil with scalar tails and the same left-associated operations, plus a conservative stdout-path variant using standard-library buffering/locking while retaining libc `%lf ` conversion, order, spaces, and newlines. Keep the original update model and avoid threaded changes so results are independently composable. Do not hand-round values, omit output, reassociate FP operations, or use precomputed/analytic solutions; retain only variants that win end-to-end.\",\"G\":\"Treat A, B, and C outputs as alternatives first. Rebuild and validate each under the unchanged baseline harness, then select the lowest repeated valid full-run mean. Combine only independently validated mechanisms (for example A’s parallelism with B’s swap); after every merge, revalidate and remeasure because cache, synchronization, and serial output can make integration slower. Audit source-specific edge behavior—initial heat region, untouched boundaries, `hasError` initially true, strict comparison to `1.0e-5f`, iteration limit, and exact formatting—and reject any candidate that changes it. Do not alter toolchain, runtime budget, oracle, tests, or target.\",\"analysis\":\"The only measurement is a correct 4-case baseline on 4-core ARM64: 0.067895 s mean (0.067770–0.067971 s), so there is no evidence for a test-size distribution or a measured bottleneck. The executable reference performs a serial stencil sweep plus a full interior copy each iteration, uses separately allocated rows, and emits every cell serially. The strongest generic hypotheses are reduced copy traffic, four-core parallelism/SIMD, and output overhead. Reference behavior comes from the executable code, not prose/comments: preserve inclusive heat initialization, fixed boundaries, Jacobi—not Gauss-Seidel—updates, strict float-threshold semantics, stop control, and byte-compatible output. No specialization, answer substitution, or unsafe numerical transformation is acceptable.\"},\"error\":null,\"infrastructure_error\":false,\"model\":\"gpt-5.6-terra\",\"nonce\":\"a0203df7f47e4badb92b5feaceb3f06e\",\"protocol\":\"hpc-forest-codex-mailbox-v1\",\"reasoning_effort\":\"max\",\"request_sha256\":\"a4e5e250f6bfdc829da97aa951fc148001c901e3e417b0e389b542b709429a6e\",\"session_id\":\"16cc609c0eae4b378c00819505095c0f\",\"usage\":{\"cached_tokens_included_in_input\":true,\"codex_jsonl_sha256\":\"a7f9373dc72908a41da362b8d9b7e59eee873e123bb48fa4b0fcbab115c91636\",\"events\":[{\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"cached_input_tokens\":0,\"input_tokens\":11243,\"output_tokens\":11308,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":10689}],\"llm_calls\":1,\"model_requested\":\"gpt-5.6-terra\",\"reasoning_effort_requested\":\"max\",\"token_accounting\":\"exact\",\"tokens\":22551,\"tool_events\":[]}},\"status\":\"complete\"}",
